04:55.864 --> 05:00.914
If you're not a great detective,
then what <i>are</i> you?

05:04.754 --> 05:06.464
You said you're looking for someone?

05:06.844 --> 05:08.924
Will you be the detective for my case?

05:10.074 --> 05:13.324
I won't ever be a detective, but...

05:13.324 --> 05:14.254
But what?

05:15.014 --> 05:17.134
If you'll take an assistant,
I'll do it.

05:17.454 --> 05:18.764
Uh, what?

05:19.344 --> 05:22.224
So who are you looking for?

05:24.004 --> 05:25.184
That's the thing.

05:25.804 --> 05:30.154
I need you to figure 
out who I'm looking for.

05:30.644 --> 05:31.384
What?

05:35.854 --> 05:40.034
There's somebody I just have to meet,

05:40.434 --> 05:44.254
but I've got no clue who it is.

05:44.254 --> 05:49.404
I don't know their age, gender,
location, or anything.

05:50.634 --> 05:56.034
Let's call our subject "X",
at least for now.

05:56.494 --> 05:59.514
You don't know anything about X?

05:59.994 --> 06:00.954
I don't.

06:00.954 --> 06:04.794
I don't even know
why I care about X.

06:05.264 --> 06:09.564
I get these sudden urges to see X.

06:10.324 --> 06:12.904
Around what time did this start?

06:13.454 --> 06:14.734
A year ago.

06:15.484 --> 06:17.444
What happened one year ago?

06:18.444 --> 06:21.454
I was about to die, but I didn't.

06:22.124 --> 06:24.164
Or well, I was given my life.

06:25.444 --> 06:29.624
The heartbeat I let you listen to
in the classroom— that's not mine.

06:30.284 --> 06:32.964
You had a heart transplant.

06:33.674 --> 06:36.704
I've had serious heart issues
ever since I was a kid.

06:36.704 --> 06:40.554
I've been in and out of hospitals,
waiting for the day I'd get a transplant.

06:40.974 --> 06:44.864
One year ago, a donor was finally found,

06:44.864 --> 06:47.394
and I was able to
undergo the procedure.

06:48.134 --> 06:53.104
Ever since then,
I've randomly had thoughts of X.

06:53.684 --> 06:54.794
It all works out.

06:55.794 --> 06:57.194
Memory transference.

06:57.594 --> 06:58.404
Huh?

06:58.404 --> 07:04.494
The X in question is somebody who
the heart's original owner wants to see.

07:04.494 --> 07:05.954
That's the most insane—

07:05.954 --> 07:10.544
If you think so, why even bother
telling me about your heart transplant?

07:12.244 --> 07:16.734
Although the phenomenon of memory
transference isn't scientifically proven,

07:16.734 --> 07:19.264
there have been a number of
cases where, after surgery,

07:19.264 --> 07:21.224
the recipient was influenced
by the organ donor.

07:21.634 --> 07:24.074
They'd start to like foods they hated,

07:24.074 --> 07:27.514
have memories of places
they'd never even visited.

07:28.194 --> 07:29.384
So what?

07:29.384 --> 07:34.234
You're saying it's the heart that
wants to meet X, not me?

07:34.584 --> 07:35.954
Probably.

07:35.954 --> 07:40.424
So X is likely someone
who was close to the donor during their life.

07:40.424 --> 07:44.244
A family member, a lover, a friend.

07:45.594 --> 07:46.874
Right...

07:47.514 --> 07:49.834
Well, glad that worked out.

07:49.834 --> 07:52.414
Problem solved.

07:53.044 --> 07:53.704
Huh?

07:53.704 --> 07:54.924
Where do you think you're going?

07:55.304 --> 07:57.434
That's all there is to this, isn't there?

07:57.434 --> 08:01.804
It's not you who wants to meet X,
it's the heart's owner.

08:02.294 --> 08:05.494
It's not a memory from your life,
so it really has nothing to do with you.

08:05.494 --> 08:06.474
It totally does!

08:06.884 --> 08:10.624
It's not just
a memory, it's a regret!

08:10.624 --> 08:13.654
Even after they passed this heart on to me,

08:13.654 --> 08:16.074
they still want to see
X that much!

08:16.074 --> 08:20.924
Their heart gave me life,
so I have to pay them back.

08:20.924 --> 08:23.864
I want to let this heart meet X.

08:24.584 --> 08:25.994
So it's just to satisfy your own desires.

08:26.314 --> 08:28.484
That's right, it's all for me.

08:28.484 --> 08:30.414
This heart is mine.

08:30.414 --> 08:32.124
So I want to meet them!

08:32.464 --> 08:35.054
That's not what you just said.

08:35.054 --> 08:36.464
Shut it!

08:40.464 --> 08:42.124
It doesn't matter. Help me.

08:42.124 --> 08:44.264
I'm not doing this for free, am I?

08:44.714 --> 08:48.014
You already got to touch my boobs.
That's more than enough, isn't it?

08:48.284 --> 08:50.154
That's basically extortion.

08:57.254 --> 08:58.234
Sorry for the wait.

09:06.584 --> 09:11.884
You shouldn't gawk at
someone you're not dating like that.{Holy shit the leadoff on this fucking line LMFAOOOOO}

09:12.264 --> 09:17.294
That's rich coming from the girl who
let a rando motorboat her.

09:18.464 --> 09:20.174
You liked it, though.

09:25.214 --> 09:27.344
You're really pushing it now.

09:29.114 --> 09:34.314
Oh no, I was looking at your uh,
collarbones. Definitely not your boobs.

09:34.584 --> 09:35.564
Weirdo.

09:35.564 --> 09:38.394
Look at my boobs
like a normal person.

09:38.864 --> 09:42.254
You've got great collarbones for your age.

09:42.254 --> 09:45.554
How do those even relate at all!

09:47.074 --> 09:50.154
This conversation is giving me déjà-vu.

09:50.154 --> 09:54.294
Yikes. Imagine having this
conversation more than once; I'd rather die.

09:54.764 --> 09:57.044
Well, shall we get going—?

09:58.294 --> 09:59.734
Get that guy!

09:59.734 --> 10:00.714
He's a thief!

10:00.714 --> 10:01.634
What?

10:06.474 --> 10:07.064
Uhh...

10:09.544 --> 10:10.664
Yeesh.

10:10.664 --> 10:12.474
You again, you little shit?

10:16.944 --> 10:21.024
You're involved in like 70% of
the crimes that happen here.

10:21.024 --> 10:24.114
Just how I'm wired.

10:24.664 --> 10:25.714
And?

10:25.714 --> 10:27.494
You're riding solo now?

10:27.494 --> 10:31.194
Nah, I'm useless like that,
especially when it comes to them.

10:31.194 --> 10:35.084
Though it seems like I'm
off their radar for now.

10:35.084 --> 10:37.904
Wow, you're brutal.

10:37.904 --> 10:40.044
The dead tell no tales, eh?

10:42.224 --> 10:42.924
Ow!

10:42.924 --> 10:44.874
What was that for?

10:44.874 --> 10:46.704
Felt like it.

10:47.144 --> 10:48.424
So, who's...

10:49.004 --> 10:51.504
Right, this is Ms. Fuubi.

10:53.644 --> 10:55.014
Kase Fuubi.

10:55.704 --> 10:58.394
You're police, right?

10:58.394 --> 11:00.474
She's an assistant inspector.

11:00.474 --> 11:03.544
And also who we're meeting.

11:04.734 --> 11:07.694
Ms. Fuubi, she's the friend
I wanted to talk to you about.

11:07.694 --> 11:09.244
Your girlfriend?

11:09.244 --> 11:10.654
No, that's not what I said.

11:11.344 --> 11:12.844
Nice to meet you!

11:12.844 --> 11:14.874
I'm Natsunagi Nagisa.

11:15.584 --> 11:19.584
Why come talk to me?

11:20.414 --> 11:23.254
Knowing you, I was pretty sure
you could do something.

11:23.254 --> 11:24.224
Dumbass.

11:24.224 --> 11:26.174
What do you think I can do?

11:26.744 --> 11:30.424
You're not just police, you're you.

11:30.794 --> 11:33.014
What's the difference?

11:33.594 --> 11:34.704
Your resolve.

11:40.434 --> 11:44.254
Right, okay.

11:44.254 --> 11:47.124
We're not doctors though.

11:47.124 --> 11:48.444
Take it up with someone else.

11:48.844 --> 11:50.184
Please!

11:50.184 --> 11:51.264
I really need to—

11:51.264 --> 11:52.264
And also,

11:53.264 --> 11:54.994
I'm busy.

11:55.464 --> 11:58.374
After this, I have plans to show my face at the big house.

11:59.164 --> 12:00.204
The big house.{holy shit this timing}

12:02.224 --> 12:07.614
If you two happened to follow me,

12:07.614 --> 12:09.214
well, that's none of my business.

12:15.514 --> 12:20.064
Listen, I've got some work
to finish off upstairs.

12:20.064 --> 12:22.734
I'm out of here in twenty,
so keep that in mind.

12:26.644 --> 12:27.774
Got it?

12:28.114 --> 12:29.024
Yes.

12:31.744 --> 12:37.784
Uh hey, bit late I know, but I swear
we were going to some "big house".

12:38.434 --> 12:40.414
This is definitely...

12:40.854 --> 12:41.954
It's a prison, ain't it.

12:41.954 --> 12:43.594
The hell you mean "ain't it"?

12:43.594 --> 12:46.034
We're supposed to be at a big house!

12:46.034 --> 12:48.034
It's slang, damn it!

12:48.034 --> 12:49.424
B-bang?

12:49.424 --> 12:51.694
What's the deal?

12:52.714 --> 12:53.874
Let's go.

12:53.874 --> 12:57.654
We're going
all the way to the end.

13:01.934 --> 13:03.424
Who's here?

13:03.424 --> 13:04.394
Some old man.

13:04.394 --> 13:05.994
Be serious.

13:05.994 --> 13:08.234
Some old man who abandoned his humanity.

13:08.234 --> 13:09.454
Would you—?

13:14.664 --> 13:17.954
Oh wow. It's been a while,

13:19.084 --> 13:20.534
ace detective.

13:20.664 --> 13:24.414
Unfortunately, I'm no ace detective.

13:25.984 --> 13:31.134
Oh yeah, you were, um, Watson, right?

13:31.544 --> 13:34.254
Your eyes still work or what?

13:35.194 --> 13:39.684
Nope, we've got the same eyes now, Watson.
Like a dead fish.

13:40.354 --> 13:43.314
Wow, that sucks a lot.

13:43.314 --> 13:46.024
Also, please stop calling me that.

13:47.724 --> 13:50.614
What, not an assistant anymore?

13:58.064 --> 14:00.454
We came here to talk to you, Bat.

14:00.814 --> 14:03.044
There's no way you'd come here to see me

14:03.044 --> 14:06.294
if there's nothing special going on.

14:06.824 --> 14:08.924
This is a great time-waster.

14:09.384 --> 14:10.584
Tell me all about it.

14:12.004 --> 14:12.944
Gotcha.

14:14.744 --> 14:15.674
What's up?

14:17.514 --> 14:20.134
You seem nervous.

14:20.134 --> 14:21.694
That's not like you.

14:21.694 --> 14:23.224
What're you talking about?

14:27.284 --> 14:29.254
I'll introduce you.

14:29.734 --> 14:32.184
This is Natsunagi Nagisa.

14:32.634 --> 14:33.774
We're in the same year at school.

14:34.364 --> 14:36.734
Natsunagi... Nagisa?

14:38.624 --> 14:39.754
Nice to meet you.

14:39.754 --> 14:41.204
I'm Natsunagi.

14:42.264 --> 14:47.404
I came today to ask you about my heart.

14:59.884 --> 15:01.084
I see.

15:01.474 --> 15:06.104
You're asking if I happen to know
anything about that heart's owner?

15:06.544 --> 15:08.484
Yes, that's it.

15:08.484 --> 15:10.304
That's it, but...

15:11.314 --> 15:15.144
Natsunagi, he's not a guy with what
you'd call an ordinary background.

15:15.724 --> 15:19.674
And while I'm at it,
he's not even an ordinary human being.

15:19.674 --> 15:20.244
Huh?

15:20.864 --> 15:25.944
Bat is an android produced
by the covert organization SPES.

15:26.864 --> 15:27.564
Uh, what?

15:28.234 --> 15:29.904
Sounds fake, huh?

15:29.904 --> 15:32.554
Duh! What kind of sci-fi fantasy bull—

15:32.554 --> 15:34.504
It's a big world.

15:34.504 --> 15:37.274
Lots of stuff out there.

15:40.294 --> 15:44.794
I can hear people talking up to
100 kilometres away, if I want.

15:45.344 --> 15:49.224
Hearing the sound of your heart is
a cakewalk, young lady.

15:49.964 --> 15:53.134
This dude flew all over the world,
weaponizing his ear.

15:53.134 --> 15:56.104
So I thought there was a chance

15:56.104 --> 16:00.284
that he may have met
your heart's previous owner.

16:01.214 --> 16:06.494
I didn't want to hide anything,
but I know this guy pretty well.

16:06.494 --> 16:08.124
Seems like it.

16:09.994 --> 16:14.334
Oh man, it's been four years since
my little scrap with you two.

16:15.584 --> 16:17.084
You two?

16:17.534 --> 16:19.304
How nostalgic!

16:19.874 --> 16:25.114
So like, there's no way I want
that ear listening to my heart.

16:25.114 --> 16:26.764
Yeah, I get it.

16:27.154 --> 16:28.754
Oh, come on.

16:28.754 --> 16:32.184
To hear the sound of your
heart, this distance is close enough.

16:32.184 --> 16:37.064
Or should I say, I've already
identified your heart, sweety.

16:37.404 --> 16:38.314
Huh?

16:38.864 --> 16:45.404
Bat, are you saying you've
met the owner of her heart?

16:45.734 --> 16:49.994
Why bother explaining when
I can just do this!

16:55.534 --> 16:56.764
So that means...

17:05.014 --> 17:06.514
Siesta!

17:07.054 --> 17:11.104
You'll never be able to raise
that tentacle against me again.

17:11.504 --> 17:14.994
I've been a detective ever since I was born.

17:17.384 --> 17:24.244
Stop it... please stop.
You can't... don't do this to me.

17:25.674 --> 17:26.704
I'm not your—

17:26.704 --> 17:30.164
Denial is never a good look, Watson.

17:32.344 --> 17:36.964
I thought she <i>was</i> the other girl.

17:39.744 --> 17:41.504
It's been a while,

17:42.704 --> 17:44.054
ace detective.

17:46.244 --> 17:48.264
So that's how it is.

17:49.584 --> 17:51.144
I thought it was weird.

17:52.134 --> 17:57.354
I'm not the type to hug a guy
I had just met like that.

17:58.464 --> 18:02.084
So it wasn't me who did that,

18:02.084 --> 18:04.574
it was this heart's owner.

18:05.084 --> 18:07.084
It was something that girl made me do—

18:07.084 --> 18:10.034
Siesta, the Sherlock to your Watson.

18:11.144 --> 18:13.994
Natsunagi, you...

18:18.624 --> 18:19.974
It's a coincidence.

18:21.064 --> 18:26.424
Meeting you, Siesta's heart being inside you.

18:26.994 --> 18:28.544
It's all just a...

18:35.274 --> 18:39.484
Was that something
she made you do too?

18:39.484 --> 18:40.944
No!

18:41.434 --> 18:43.344
That was me!

18:43.344 --> 18:45.904
I wanted to hit you, so I hit you!

18:46.384 --> 18:47.854
A coincidence?

18:47.854 --> 18:50.264
You're gonna call this a coincidence!

18:50.264 --> 18:51.704
As if!

18:51.704 --> 18:53.744
Don't you dare just dismiss this!

18:54.584 --> 18:56.294
This is desire!

18:56.294 --> 19:01.094
Even after death,
she wanted to see you, be with you!

19:01.094 --> 19:04.874
It's the only wish this heart has!

19:05.464 --> 19:09.174
Since forever, we—

19:09.594 --> 19:13.694
Kimihiko Kimizuka,
we've been looking for you!

19:13.694 --> 19:17.774
Don't you ever just call it a coincidence!

19:18.464 --> 19:21.104
These feelings are not something to throw away!

19:27.314 --> 19:28.674
Are you in there?

19:31.714 --> 19:36.574
Do you know how much I suffered
after becoming your assistant?

19:37.344 --> 19:40.744
We were fighting a supernatural organization,

19:40.744 --> 19:44.724
and for three years, we traveled the
world trying to stay alive, broke.

19:45.294 --> 19:48.254
We slept outdoors in a hurricane.

19:48.654 --> 19:52.634
We won big at a casino, celebrated like crazy,

19:53.564 --> 19:56.224
but of course, the very next day,
we were broke again.

19:56.224 --> 19:59.064
We walked through deserts,
traversed jungles,

19:59.064 --> 20:00.854
passed over mountains, and crossed oceans.

20:01.504 --> 20:04.264
And then, you just...

20:06.744 --> 20:10.444
Why did you go and die first, you idiot?

20:25.844 --> 20:28.344
I'm glad it all worked out.

20:29.094 --> 20:31.054
You can thank me all you want now.

20:31.474 --> 20:35.034
Ms. Fuubi, you knew from
the start, didn't you?

20:35.034 --> 20:36.014
Huh?

20:37.014 --> 20:38.224
About her...

20:38.534 --> 20:42.434
About who Natsunagi's
heart once belonged to.

20:44.364 --> 20:45.264
Ms. Fuubi.

20:53.054 --> 20:57.164
I'm not so cruel as to make a
young lady do actual detective work.

21:05.244 --> 21:07.434
Thanks for today.

21:08.834 --> 21:12.304
Thanks to you,
how do I put this...

21:13.244 --> 21:16.264
I couldn't go on like this,
that's what I realized.

21:17.544 --> 21:19.974
If you're saying that, then I also...

21:25.204 --> 21:26.234
Natsunagi,

21:27.214 --> 21:30.444
whoever that heart may belong to,

21:31.734 --> 21:34.954
you can live your own life.

21:37.854 --> 21:40.704
You don't need to try to replace anybody.

21:44.044 --> 21:44.804
See you around.

21:49.154 --> 21:51.384
Kimizuka, I—

21:53.314 --> 21:54.554
What is it, Natsunagi?

21:57.324 --> 21:58.634
Umm, I...

